  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Save the Sacred Forest and Build Tribal Economy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Alik Sacred Forest, is the last home of the Higa-onon indigenous people, the sacred place to exercise their beliefs and cultural traditions, and the house of endangered species.   50 ha of the Sacred Forest are threatened to be bought by a mining company. We can buy it back and preserve it for perpetuity by giving it the status of common land. Support us in preserving biodiversity and ancestral knowledge. This is the first phase of a larger vision for building a tribal economy.</narrative>
  </description>
